==English==

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|sa|विष्णु|tr=Víṣṇu}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈvɪʃnu/}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# {{lb|en|Hinduism}} One of the [[Trimurti]] (trinity) in Hindu [[mythology]], and the most popularly venerated god in [[Hinduism]]. Vishnu is commonly depicted as being [[blue]] in colour and having four arms: with each hand holding either a [[lotus]], a [[mace]], a [[conch]] shell or [[Chakra]] weapon. Vishnu is the [[supreme|Supreme]] [[being]] or Ultimate Reality for [[Vaishnavas]] and a manifestation of [[Brahman]] in the [[Advaita]] or [[Smarta]] traditions of Hinduism.
# {{given name|en|male|from=Sanskrit}} used in India.

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|Narayana}}

